---
title: Tartlet Shells
yield: 12 shells
---

Roll out the @./components/1-2-3-cookie-dough{570%g} ~{0.3%cm} thick. Using a #10-cm cutter{}, cut 12 rounds.

Assemble the shells on a #parchment-lined sheet pan{}. Fit the rounds into #7.5-cm tartlet rings or pans{}, pressing the dough into place against the sides. Smooth and trim the top edges.

Place the shells under refrigeration or in the freezer until very firm. Line the shells with #foil or parchment{} and fill with #pie weights or dried beans{}.

Blind bake at 191°C until the shells have just begun to brown, about ~{20%minutes}.

Remove the foil or parchment and weights. Lightly brush the pastry with @egg wash{as needed}. Bake until golden brown, about ~{10%minutes} longer.